---
source: crates/assertrust/tests/cli.rs
expression: run.stdout
---
Replay a branch's history as CI would have checked it: each merged PR, each push

Usage: assertrust backtest [OPTIONS]

Options:
      --range <RANGE>
          The commits to replay: BASE..HEAD, those on HEAD's first-parent line after BASE

      --last <N>
          Replay the last N commits on the current branch's first-parent line (default: 100, or the labels file's range)

      --labels <FILE>
          A file with a verdict on each finding, to measure assertrust: prints how often it's right, and exits with 1 on findings not labelled yet or no longer found

      --update-labels
          Add new findings to the labels file, not labelled yet, and drop false alarms no longer found

      --format <FORMAT>
          Output format

          Possible values:
          - terminal: Short, human-readable findings, by PR and push
          - json:     Machine-readable findings, for scripts and other tools
          
          [default: terminal]

      --show-transient
          Also show weakening that was undone later in the same PR

  -v, --verbose
          Show the test name, before/after snippets, the full commit message, and changed outcomes

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')
